& [ComposedAgentIdentity] answers what a game agent being a Cantor instance should mean
  + [CantorAgentInstance] is one stable commissioned logical identity with a purpose, semantic-state cursor, program set, authority projection, episode cursor, and lifecycle
  + [inference_provider] is an optional replaceable model or deterministic reasoner used by the instance
  + [embodiment] is a revocable binding to one environment entity or control endpoint for one bounded session
  + [environment_adapter] translates typed environment observations and proposed actions without owning semantic authority
  + [effect_broker] alone commits an admitted game action under explicit capability
  = conclusion: the game agent may be presented as a Cantor instance, but the complete runtime is Cantor semantics plus provider, adapter, effect broker, and embodiment binding
  - never: treat the Cantor query engine alone as an autonomous embodied agent

& [ExistingSupportMap] distinguishes reuse from new work
  + [resident_multiplexing] is partial because cantord shares one immutable generation across callers but sessions and per-agent durable cursors are explicitly deferred
  + [participant_identity_and_addressing] is supported by ParticipantAddress, CommissionContract, WorkPacket, authority containment, and exact correlation
  + [bounded_deliberation] is supported by immutable messages, replay defense, deterministic budgets, Observer review, and typed faults
  + [semantic_reentry] is formed by TransportableSemanticState but has no embodied-session implementation authority
  + [learning_governance] is formed by LearningToAttendCycle, candidate learning artifacts, held-out comparison, signed admission, and rollback
  + [program_activation] is formed by the Narrative Cantor registry and bounded call graph
  + [multi_agent_exchange] is formed by the Cooperative Inference Junction but remains implementation-deferred
  + [embodied_binding] is absent
  + [environment_observation_action_effect_protocol] is absent
  + [episode_and_skill_evidence] is absent
  + [Minecraft_adapter] is absent
  + [population_experiment_protocol] is absent

& [EmbodiedFeatureProgram] is the candidate dependency graph
  + [CEA-001] is Cantor embodied-agent identity, instance multiplexing, embodiment binding, release, resume, and reentry forms
  + [CEA-002] is provider-neutral environment identity, capability discovery, observation, action proposal, admission, commitment, and effect-report contracts
  + [CEA-003] is append-only episode causal ledger for goal, precondition observation, decision, action, effect, outcome, fault, and provenance
  + [CEA-004] is demonstration-to-skill candidate compilation with applicability boundaries, counterexamples, cost, risk, evidence, and no self-admission
  + [CEA-005] is replay, held-out, adversarial, and supervisor review that may sign a scoped SkillPattern while retaining rollback
  + [CEA-006] is a deterministic effect-free embodied mock loop proving CEA-001 through CEA-005 before a live game adapter
  + [CEA-007] is a Minecraft-specific NeoForge adapter and effect broker owned by the Minecraft integration boundary rather than Cantor core
  + [CEA-008] is a population experiment harness for dozens of stable agents, isolated and shared memory policies, cohorts, metrics, reproducibility, and safety
  + [CEA-009] is optional learned skill or attention routing in shadow mode under the existing neural-routing adoption gate
  = must: treat these identifiers as architecture candidates until separately preserved and processed through SJS

& [SkillPatternDataDesign] gives precise meaning to learning tricks and patterns
  + [DemonstrationEpisode] is immutable environment version, agent identity, body binding, goal, initial observation digest, ordered decisions, committed actions, observed effects, outcome measures, faults, and source provenance
  + [SkillCandidate] is an unsigned generalization containing purpose, preconditions, applicability boundary, action template, expected effects, stop conditions, resource cost, risks, evidence episodes, counterexamples, confidence, and unresolved questions
  + [SkillPattern] is a reviewed and signed SkillCandidate with exact scope, version, evaluation result, limitations, rollback target, and invalidation conditions
  + [SkillInvocation] binds one SkillPattern version to one current goal, observation, capability grant, embodiment session, expected effect, and result trace
  + [learning_signal] is repeatable task outcome, correction load, action cost, failure rate, safety violations, transfer performance, and semantic proof coverage
  = must: preserve observation, inference, proposed action, authorized action, actual effect, and later interpretation as distinct records
  = must: preserve failed episodes and counterexamples as first-class evidence
  - never: turn one successful behavior, fluent explanation, or high correlation weight directly into an authorized skill

& [MinecraftAdapterBoundary] is strict
  + [inside_Cantor] is identities, purposes, semantic state, programs, commissions, action proposals, authority checks, episode and skill evidence, review, and proof
  + [inside_Minecraft_integration] is NeoForge APIs, entity lookup, world observations, game tick correlation, command translation, server compatibility, and action execution
  + [shared_contract] is versioned observation, capability, action, effect, health, and fault envelopes
  + [server_authority] must remain distinct from an individual agent capability
  + [player_and_world_safety] requires explicit protected-player, protected-region, inventory, command, rate, resource, and rollback policy before live action
  - never: put Minecraft block, item, entity, tick, or NeoForge implementation types into Cantor core machine forms
  - never: let an LLM response call the game server without EffectBroker admission and durable accounting

& [FirstSelectedFeature] is CEA-001 only
  + [candidate_profile] is cantor-embodied-agent-identity-binding/0.1
  + [reason] is dozens of logical agents cannot safely observe, learn, resume, or act until stable agent identity is separated from replaceable provider jobs and revocable game embodiment
  + [candidate_forms] are EmbodiedAgentIdentity, EnvironmentIdentity, EmbodimentEndpointIdentity, EmbodimentSessionIdentity, EmbodimentBindingClaim, BindingLifecycle, SemanticStateCursor, EpisodeCursor, and typed faults
  + [candidate_lifecycle] is unbound, binding_proposed, bound, suspended, released, expired, or faulted
  + [candidate_authority] is pure representation and validation only
  + [dependency_delta] is zero
  + [effect_delta] is zero
  + [implementation_authority] is absent until a fresh source document completes SJS and receives a valid satisfaction signature

& [CandidateDependencyOrder] is conservative
  + [edge] is CEA-001 before any embodied observation or action
  + [edge] is CEA-001 and CEA-002 before CEA-003
  + [edge] is CEA-003 before CEA-004 and CEA-005
  + [edge] is CEA-001 through CEA-005 before CEA-006
  + [edge] is CEA-006 plus Minecraft-side signed adapter authority before CEA-007
  + [edge] is repeatable single-agent proof before CEA-008
  + [edge] is a reviewed corpus and deterministic baseline before CEA-009

& [VerificationFrontier] is measurable
  + stable agent identity survives provider replacement and embodiment release-resume without conflating old and new sessions
  + two agents cannot simultaneously acquire one exclusive embodiment endpoint under one environment policy
  + stale state, stale capability, expired binding, wrong environment, wrong body, replay, and identity collision fail closed
  + one recorded episode round-trips with complete causal and provenance lineage
  + one SkillCandidate is accepted only after replay and held-out evidence and another is rejected with preserved counterexample
  + deterministic mock proof precedes every Minecraft-side effect
  + population metrics distinguish individual adaptation, shared-corpus transfer, correlated failure, and contamination

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - no bot process, Minecraft connection, NeoForge mod, server command, player impersonation, world mutation, inventory mutation, movement, combat, chat, model launch, learned router, database mutation, or external effect is authorized by this intake
  - no current M2B authority is superseded or delayed by this parked feature program
  - no candidate CEA requirement may be marked supported until its own source, canonical specification, implementation, tests, proof, and fault behavior exist

